## Description

This analytic provides a high-level overview of **process execution frequency** by counting how many times each executable has been observed within the Sysmon dataset.

Unlike signature-based detections that search for specific attacker techniques, this detection is designed for **behavioral analysis, baselining, and threat hunting**. It enables analysts to understand which executables are most frequently used within the environment and identify uncommon or unexpected processes that may warrant investigation.

This type of analysis is commonly performed during proactive threat hunting and security monitoring.

