# Analyst Notes

Process frequency analysis is a foundational threat hunting technique used to establish normal operating baselines within an environment. By understanding which processes execute most frequently, defenders can quickly identify unusual binaries, rare administrative tools, or Living-off-the-Land Binaries (LOLBins) that may indicate malicious activity.

Unlike traditional signature-based detections, this analytic does not alert on a single event. Instead, it provides valuable operational context that supports anomaly detection, hypothesis-driven hunting, and long-term behavioral monitoring.

